  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Eastern Air Express has $224M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Eastern Air Express has 61 awards this fiscal year, with an average award size of $3.7M and obligations up 3870.1% year over year. Eastern Air Express received no obligations in FY21, $3.3K in FY22, $2.9M in FY23, $2.2M in FY24, $5.6M in FY25, and $224M in FY26. Eastern Air Express is primarily buying from the Department of Homeland Security, which obligated $216M, followed by the Department of Defense with $5.6M and the Department of the Interior with $3M. Eastern Air Express obligations reported here are contract obligations; largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables would report total contract values where applicable. Eastern Air Express current-year totals are partial because they reflect fiscal year to date activity. Eastern Air Express shows a concentrated FY2026 buying pattern driven by one or a few large obligations from the Department of Homeland Security, while earlier fiscal years show much smaller annual totals.",
