        "heading": "Why did obligations jump so much in FY2026?",
        "body": "Eastern Air Express obligations rose to $224M in FY26 after totals of $5.6M in FY25 and smaller amounts in prior years. Eastern Air Express recorded a year-over-year change up 3870.1%, reflecting a dramatic increase in FY26 obligations. Eastern Air Express concentration of $216M in obligations from the Department of Homeland Security explains most of the FY26 increase."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the top buying agencies and how concentrated are they?",
        "body": "The Department of Homeland Security is the largest buyer, with $216M in obligations to Eastern Air Express in FY26. The Department of Defense obligated $5.6M and the Department of the Interior obligated $3M. The top buyer accounts for the vast majority of Eastern Air Express FY26 obligations, while other agencies account for the remainder."
      }
